POD mosquito  cannot tolerate taint Martein on the nodes

controlplane ~ ➜  kubectl describe node node01 | grep -i taints
Taints:             spray=mortein:NoSchedule

#4 Create another pod named bee with the nginx image, which has a toleration set to the taint mortein.
Image name: nginx |Key: spray | Value: mortein | Effect: NoSchedule | Status: Running

controlplane ~ ➜  cat bee.yaml
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: bee
spec:
  containers:
  - image: nginx
    name: bee
  tolerations:
  - key: spray
    value: mortein
    effect: NoSchedule
    operator: Equal

controlplane ~ ➜  

Observe that the bee pod has been scheduled on node node01 due to the toleration that has been configured for the pod.

controlplane ~ ➜  kubectl get pods -o wide
NAME       READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE     IP           NODE     NOMINATED NODE   READINESS GATES
bee        1/1     Running   0          9s      172.17.1.2   node01   <none>           <none>
mosquito   0/1     Pending   0          6m27s   <none>       <none>   <none>           <none>

#5 Remove the taint on controlplane, which currently has the taint effect of NoSchedule.



controlplane ~ ➜  kubectl taint nodes controlplane node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane:NoSchedule-
node/controlplane untainted



After remove the taint, pod mosquito hosted in controlplane

controlplane ~ ➜  kubectl get pods -o wide
NAME       READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE   IP           NODE           NOMINATED NODE   READINESS GATES
